# PAM configuration for veiland's fingerprint unlock (all distros).
# Used only when the user sets `[fingerprint] enabled = true`. veiland
# runs it in parallel with the password check, never answers a password
# prompt on it, and only accepts a success after the module has asked
# for a finger.
# Only pam_fprintd, on purpose. Don't include fingerprint-auth or
# system-auth: Fedora's fingerprint-auth runs pam_faillock after a failed
# scan, and veiland restarts the scan after each 30 s timeout, so it
# would lock the account while the screen sits idle.
auth     required  pam_fprintd.so
